#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit functions {#circuit-functions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Circuit functions simplify the execution of quantum circuits by abstracting "
"away key steps such as transpilation, error suppression, and error "
"mitigation. Researchers using Circuit functions can focus on developing and "
"evaluating quantum algorithms without needing to manage the complexities of "
"optimizing circuits for quantum hardware. Circuit functions accept circuit-"
"oriented inputs, such as PUB (Primitive Unified Bloc) objects, and return "
"results such as mitigated expectation values. They can also serve as "
"building blocks for creating higher-level, customized quantum "
"applications.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Functions are an experimental feature available only to IBM Quantum&reg; Premium Plan, Flex Plan, and On-Prem (via IBM Quantum Platform API) Plan users. Refer to [Set up IBM Quantum Functions](/guides/functions-get-started) for instructions on getting access.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

